<div class="page-wrap prose">
  <section id="question" aria-labelledby="question-title">
    <h2 id="question-title">The question</h2>
    <p>
      Your CDC events arrive twice, or out of order. What does your warehouse or lakehouse do with them, and what do you
      have to set? CDC delivery is at-least-once, and
      end-to-end exactly-once across independent systems is not achievable in general. What you can reach is
      <strong>exactly-once processing</strong> (see <a href="{{ '/glossary/' | url }}#effectively-once">effectively-once</a>): at-least-once transport into an
      <a href="{{ '/glossary/' | url }}#idempotent-write">idempotent sink</a> keyed on the primary key and ordered by the
      <strong>source log position</strong> (<a href="{{ '/glossary/' | url }}#lsn-scn">LSN, SCN or binlog coordinate</a>),
      with deletes kept as <strong>delete markers</strong>.
    </p>
    <p class="callout">
      Every target below has a way to say &ldquo;this column decides which version wins&rdquo;. Several default to
      something else: arrival order, commit order or a timestamp. The job is to name three things for your target: the
      <strong>key</strong>, the <strong>ordering column</strong> (the log position) and the <strong>delete marker</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prerequisites:
      <a href="{{ '/event-envelope/' | url }}#ordering-title">Event envelope</a>,
      <a href="{{ '/materialization/' | url }}#merge-title">Materialization 101</a> and
      <a href="{{ '/partitioning/' | url }}#recon">Making sinks bulletproof</a>, which explains why a timestamp, a
      Kafka offset or <code>ts_ms</code> is the wrong version and how to compare positions. This page does not repeat
      that argument; it maps it onto six products.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Everything here was checked by reading each vendor&rsquo;s documentation on 2026-10-09 (links at the end). Nothing
      was run against a live product. Where a behaviour is not stated in the pages read, the text says
      &ldquo;check your version&rdquo; instead of guessing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="at-a-glance-title">
    <h2 id="at-a-glance-title">The six targets at a glance</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto" role="region" aria-label="Six targets compared" tabindex="0" data-table-scroll>
    <table>
