    <p>
      The pattern is the same everywhere: land the source position as a column, make it the ordering input, and keep the
      delete as a row that remembers its position. The rest of this page is the per-target detail.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="replay" aria-labelledby="replay-title">
    <h2 id="replay-title">A worked replay</h2>
    <p>
      One key, three source changes: position 100 sets <code>name = 'a'</code>, position 200 sets
      <code>name = 'b'</code>, position 300 deletes the key. Three things go wrong in practice:
      <strong>(1)</strong> the 100-batch is replayed after 200 was applied; <strong>(2)</strong> 200 arrives before 100;
      <strong>(3)</strong> 300 was applied, then 200 is replayed.
    </p>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto" role="region" aria-label="Worked replay results" tabindex="0" data-table-scroll>
    <table>
      <caption>Resulting row per target. Derived by reading the documentation, not by running any product.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Target and ordering input</th>
          <th scope="col">(1) Old batch replayed</th>
          <th scope="col">(2) Swapped arrival</th>
          <th scope="col">(3) Update after delete</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">BigQuery, no sequence number</th>
          <td><code>a</code> (stale)</td>
          <td><code>a</code> (stale)</td>
          <td>Row returns</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">BigQuery, position as sequence number</th>
          <td><code>b</code></td>
          <td><code>b</code></td>
          <td>Stays deleted; beyond the 2-day delete window: check</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Databricks, <code>SEQUENCE BY</code> position</th>
          <td><code>b</code></td>
          <td><code>b</code></td>
          <td>Stays deleted while the tombstone is kept (2 days by default)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Hudi, no ordering field</th>
          <td><code>a</code> (stale)</td>
          <td><code>a</code> (stale)</td>
          <td>Row returns</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Hudi, ordering field = position</th>
          <td><code>b</code></td>
          <td><code>b</code></td>
          <td>Check your version; use a marker column to be safe</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Iceberg Flink upsert (no guard)</th>
          <td><code>a</code> (stale)</td>
          <td><code>a</code> (stale)</td>
          <td>Row returns</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Iceberg <code>MERGE INTO</code> with position guard and marker</th>
          <td><code>b</code></td>
          <td><code>b</code></td>
          <td>Stays deleted</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Delta or Snowflake <code>MERGE</code>, no guard</th>
          <td><code>a</code> (stale)</td>
          <td><code>a</code> (stale)</td>
          <td>Row returns (no match, so it is inserted)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Delta or Snowflake <code>MERGE</code> with position guard and marker</th>
