  <section id="monday" aria-labelledby="monday-title">
    <h2 id="monday-title">What to do Monday</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>For each target you load, write down the key, the ordering input and the delete representation. If the ordering input is arrival, commit order or a timestamp, that is your finding.</li>
      <li>Carry the source position (and an ordinal for changes that share one) into the landing data. Compare it numerically, never as text.</li>
      <li>Set it as the ordering input: <code>_CHANGE_SEQUENCE_NUMBER</code>, <code>SEQUENCE BY</code>, the Hudi ordering field, or the <code>MERGE</code> guard.</li>
      <li>Keep deletes as markers with a position. Find out how long your target remembers a delete and compare it with how far back you can replay.</li>
      <li>Replay one old batch and one swapped pair in staging and check the final rows against the table above.</li>
      <li>Mark every &ldquo;check your version&rdquo; item above as an owner and a test, not an assumption.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

